      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 47. वादि &c.—Mr. Telang proposes that this adj. and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "विनीतोचिता should denote two kinds of learning and quotes the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "subhashita विद्या विवादाय धनं मदाय &c. to support his position.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "There, however, two kinds of persons are specially mentioned",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "as possessing two kinds of learning. Here we have no mention",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "made of two persons of different temperaments as in the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "subhâshita; but the adj. विनीतोचिता seems to have been purposely",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "added to signify that the kind of learning meant here is not",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "that which falls under the category (खलस्य) विद्या विवादाय. High",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "learning is capable of putting down an antagonist, but it need",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "not at the same time be prone to controversy when it is posses-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "sed by good men. करिकुम्भ०—i. e. the elephants of the enemy.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "तारुण्य which is the fittest period of life for achieving the three",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "things mentioned in the foregone lines.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 48. शुश्रूषा—properly desire to hear; hence ‘service,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "attendance.’ समाहितं-सम्यक् आहितं firmly placed, concentrated,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "devoted. पित्रोः—एकशेषद्वंद्व; माता च पिता च पितरौ; by पिता मात्रा ।",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "Pán. 1, 2. 70; also (मातापितरौ) तयोः । पर &c.—coveting a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "morsel of food from others. काकैरिव—Cf. supra Sl. 46 and. भुक्तं",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "मानविवर्जितं परगृहेष्वाशंकया काकवत् । Sl. 4.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 49. परिगताः—died; cf. परिगतः V. l. Veni. III. अपगताः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "is simpler. To explain गमिताः Ràmarshi adds कालेनेति शेषः. This",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "will do very well. But Mr. Telang thinks गमित to be an in-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "stance of स्वार्थे णिच् and refers for a parallel instance to Rag. II.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "50 In the passage referred to, however, the causal sense is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "not at all justifiable, which is not the case in the present passage.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "सिकतिल &c.—see Pán. V. 2. 105. quoted in the com; चादण्",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "मतुप् च । सिकताः सन्त्यस्मिन्देशे इति सिकतिलः, सैकतः, सिकतावान् Sid.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "Kau. Fig. Upamá.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 50. तस्यार्धस्य परस्य चार्धम्—Explain तस्यार्धस्य पञ्चाशत्सं-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "ख्याकस्य अर्धस्य अर्धं सार्धद्वादश वर्षाणि (बाल्ये) पुनः तस्य परस्या-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "र्धस्यार्धं सार्धद्वादशवर्षाणि (वृद्धत्वे) इत्यर्थः । शेषं उर्वरितमायुः पञ्चविंशति-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "वर्षपरिमितमित्यर्थः । Human life extends over 100 years.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "Half of this is passed in the night, one fourth of the",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
